            <ArticleTitle>Conference scene: Parasites to treat immune-mediated diseases?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>573-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2217/imt.12.44</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A growing number of childhood diseases, such as allergic disorders (e.g., allergic rhinitis, atopic dermatitis and asthma) and other immune-mediated diseases (e.g., Type 1 diabetes), have been linked to environmental exposures during prenatal and early postnatal life, along with genetic determinants. Immunological mechanisms, diagnosis, treatment, prevention and management of allergies and other immune-mediated diseases were discussed at the 2012 Annual Meeting of the American Academy of Allergy, Asthma &amp; Immunology in Orlando, FL, USA, 2-6 March 2012.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
